<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Heinz rating is cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Heinz rating is cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Schroder Wertheim managing director Robert Cummins said Tuesday he had cut his rating on food company H.J. Heinz Co to market perform from outperform.</p>
<p>-- &quot;The reason is the stock price,&quot; Cummins said.</p>
<p>-- The share price, he said, has increased about 42 percent since last year and is up 22 percent since January 1.</p>
<p>-- The analyst said his earnings estimates remain $1.93 a share for fiscal 1997 and $2.13 for fiscal 1998.</p>
<p>-- Heinz shares were off 5/8 at 43-1/4.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
